//! Vanilla 26.2's creative-inventory tab contents.
//!
//! This table is generated by hand-transcription from the decompiled 26.2 client source at
//! `.cache/mc/26.2/client-src/net/minecraft/world/item/CreativeModeTabs.java`. Each
//! [`CreativeTab`] mirrors one `Registry.register(...)` block in `CreativeModeTabs.bootstrap`:
//! its registry id, title translation key, tab-button icon, tab-strip position (`top_row` /
//! `column`), and its `displayItems` contents in vanilla's own registration order -- order is
//! layout, so it is preserved exactly, including expansions (see below).
//!
//! ## Per-tab item counts
//!
//! - `building_blocks`: 462
//! - `colored_blocks`: 198
//! - `natural_blocks`: 247
//! - `functional_blocks`: 232
//! - `redstone_blocks`: 70
//! - `hotbar`: 0
//! - `search`: 0
//! - `tools_and_utilities`: 145
//! - `combat`: 77
//! - `food_and_drinks`: 42
//! - `ingredients`: 151
//! - `spawn_eggs`: 89
//! - `op_blocks`: 12
//! - `inventory`: 0
//! - **total: 1725**
//!
//! `hotbar`, `search` and `inventory` carry no literal list -- vanilla builds them at
//! runtime (hotbar from saved hotbars, search from the union of every other tab's search-
//! visible items, inventory from the survival inventory) -- so their `items` slice is `&[]`.
//!
//! ## Expansions applied while transcribing
//!
//! - `registerColoredItems(_, gameplayColorOrder, Items.X)` (building_blocks/colored_blocks/
//!   functional_blocks) expands to 16 entries in `gameplayColorOrder`'s own declared order
//!   (white, light_gray, gray, black, brown, red, orange, yellow, lime, green, cyan,
//!   light_blue, blue, purple, magenta, pink -- read from `CreativeModeTabs.java`, and it is
//!   neither alphabetical nor `DyeColor` ordinal order).
//! - `copperBlockFamilies(family -> family.weathering()/.waxed().forEach(...))`
//!   (building_blocks) expands to the 4 weathering stages (unaffected/exposed/weathered/
//!   oxidized) then, in a second pass over all 11 families, their 4 waxed counterparts --
//!   88 items total, for: copper_block, chiseled_copper, copper_grate, cut_copper,
//!   cut_copper_stairs, cut_copper_slab, copper_bars, copper_door, copper_trapdoor,
//!   copper_bulb, copper_chain. `copper_block` is the one family whose weathered/waxed
//!   names drop the `_block` suffix (`exposed_copper`, not `exposed_copper_block`) --
//!   confirmed against `lodestone-data`'s generated item table, not assumed.
//! - `Items.<FAMILY>.forEach(...)` on a `WeatheringCopperCollection<Item>` (functional_blocks'
//!   copper lantern/chain/bulb/golem-statue/chest, redstone_blocks' waxed copper bulb, and
//!   the lightning rod) expands to that family's 4 (or, for a bare `.forEach`, 8: 4
//!   weathering + 4 waxed) items the same way.
//! - `Items.<FAMILY>.forEach(...)` on a `ColorCollection<Item>` (`Items.DYE`, `Items.HARNESS`,
//!   `Items.DYED_BUNDLE`) expands to 16 entries, but in `ColorCollection`'s own field-
//!   declaration order (white, orange, magenta, light_blue, yellow, lime, pink, gray,
//!   light_gray, cyan, purple, blue, brown, green, red, black -- see `ColorCollection.java`'s
//!   constructor and `forEach`), which is **not** `gameplayColorOrder`. `Items.DYE.forEach`
//!   in the ingredients tab uses this order, not `gameplayColorOrder`.
//! - `Items.WOOL.white()` (redstone_blocks) -> `minecraft:white_wool`.
//! - `Items.LIGHTNING_ROD.waxed().unaffected()` (redstone_blocks) -> `minecraft:waxed_lightning_rod`.
//! - `Items.COPPER_CHEST.waxed().unaffected()` (redstone_blocks) -> `minecraft:waxed_copper_chest`.
//!   Both confirmed present in `lodestone-data`'s generated item table (not the unwaxed
//!   fallback the task brief allowed for).
//! - Two Mojang field-name quirks in `Items.java`, resolved against the generated item table:
//!   `Items.CUT_STANDSTONE_SLAB` (sic) -> `minecraft:cut_sandstone_slab`; `Items.DRY_SHORT_GRASS`
//!   / `Items.DRY_TALL_GRASS` -> `minecraft:short_dry_grass` / `minecraft:tall_dry_grass` (the
//!   real ids reverse the field name's word order).
//! - `spawn_eggs` is **not** a pure registry sweep in 26.2: besides every `*_spawn_egg`, it
//!   literally lists `minecraft:spawner`, `minecraft:trial_spawner` and
//!   `minecraft:creaking_heart`, all transcribed here in source order.
//! - `op_blocks`' `TestBlockMode` loop (4 modes: start/log/fail/accept, each stamping a
//!   component onto `Items.TEST_BLOCK`) and its light-level loop (16 levels, 15..=0, onto
//!   `Items.LIGHT`) are both skipped as component-bearing (see below), but per the task's
//!   instruction the plain base items `minecraft:test_block` and `minecraft:light` are
//!   each emitted once, in the loops' place.
//!
//! ## Deliberately skipped (component-bearing or registry-sweep families)
//!
//! These need `ItemStack` components (potion contents, firework duration, enchantment level,
//! painting variant, ...) or a live registry sweep that this static table does not model.
//! Each is dropped silently from the data below and recorded here instead:
//!
//! - `Raid.getOminousBannerInstance(...)` (functional_blocks) -- an ominous banner stack built
//!   from the banner-pattern registry.
//! - `search.acceptAll(tempItems)` (search tab) -- built at runtime from every other tab's
//!   search-visible items.
//! - `generatePresetPaintings(...)` (functional_blocks: placeable variants; op_blocks: the
//!   non-placeable variants under `hasPermissions()`) -- one stack per `PaintingVariant`,
//!   sorted by area then width.
//! - `generateFireworksAllDurations(...)` (tools_and_utilities, combat) -- one
//!   `minecraft:firework_rocket` stack per craftable duration (`FireworkRocketItem
//!   .CRAFTABLE_DURATIONS = {1, 2, 3}`).
//! - `generateInstrumentTypes(...)` (tools_and_utilities) -- one `minecraft:goat_horn` stack
//!   per instrument in the `goat_horns` tag.
//! - `generateSuspiciousStews(...)` (food_and_drinks) -- one `minecraft:suspicious_stew` per
//!   `SuspiciousEffectHolder`.
//! - `generateOminousBottles(...)` (food_and_drinks) -- 5 `minecraft:ominous_bottle` stacks,
//!   amplifier 0..=4.
//! - `generatePotionEffectTypes(...)` (combat: tipped arrows; food_and_drinks: potion/splash
//!   potion/lingering potion) -- one stack per registered `Potion`.
//! - `generateEnchantmentBookTypesOnlyMaxLevel` / `AllLevels` (ingredients) -- one
//!   `minecraft:enchanted_book` per enchantment (max level only for the tab itself, every
//!   level for the search tab).
//!
//! ## How to change it
//!
//! Re-run the transcription against a newer `CreativeModeTabs.java` if vanilla's tab layout
//! changes; there is no generator script checked in, so this file must be hand-regenerated.
//! Every id was cross-checked against `lodestone-data`'s generated
//! `crates/lodestone-data/src/generated/items.rs::ITEM_NAMES` table -- do the same for any
//! addition, since `Items.java`'s constant *names* are not always the registry id (see the
//! `CUT_STANDSTONE_SLAB` / `DRY_SHORT_GRASS` note above).

/// One creative-inventory tab: its registry id, its title translation key, the
/// item whose icon labels its button, which row/column of the tab strip it sits
/// in, and its item list in vanilla's own order.
///
/// Read by [`super::creative`], the screen this table was transcribed for.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub(crate) struct CreativeTab {
    pub(crate) id: &'static str,
    pub(crate) title_key: &'static str,
    pub(crate) icon: &'static str,
    pub(crate) top_row: bool,
    pub(crate) column: u8,
    pub(crate) items: &'static [&'static str],
}

